  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1120 AM CDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nThis hot and dry pattern is going nowhere through the end of the \nweek as this high pressure stays overhead through Friday. \nTemperatures will stay in the upper-90s through Friday with readings \ncontinuing to flirt with daily records. An extension of the Heat \nAdvisory may be needed through the end of the week. While some spots \nmay not technically hit heat advisory criteria, these forecast \ntemperatures are at least 10 degrees above normal, and this \nprolonged heat wave will make for major heat risk. The high finally \nshifts west this weekend, and temperatures will fall ever so slowly. \nA pattern change looks to finally arrive early next week as an upper-\nlevel trough tracks to the north, sending a cold front south. This \nwill finally drop temperatures below 90 degrees and reintroduce \nmedium rain chances to the forecast.",
